IMPORT prelude

-- Duties Act 2008 (Western Australia) -- transfer duty at the general rate (s 26, Schedule 2 Division 1), the first home owner
-- concessional rate (Chapter 2 Part 6 Division 3, ss 141, 142A, 142, 143; Schedule 2 Division 2), foreign transfer duty
-- (Chapter 3A Part 2: ss 205A, 205H, 205L, 205O), whether shares are dutiable property (s 15), and landholder duty on an
-- acquisition of shares in a land-rich entity (Chapter 3: ss 155(2), 161, 163, 184, 186, 188).
--
-- Edition: compilation of the Duties Act 2008 (Act No. 11 of 2008) as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49812.txt (legislation.wa.gov.au mrdoc 49812, retrieved 2026-09-07). The deposit states no
-- compilation number or date; the last entry in its compilation table is the Help to Buy (Commonwealth Powers) Act 2025 Pt. 4
-- Div. 1 (in operation 19 Dec 2025), and it lists the Retirement Villages Amendment Act 2024 Pt. 3 as in operation 1 Sep 2026.
-- The last numbered reprint it names is Reprint 3 (as at 13 Nov 2015).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. au/wa:REQ-0004 (subjects/au/wa/requirements.jsonl), priority 1, raised 9 times by the three Western Australian
-- cradle-to-grave lives: Chloe c051 (a $620,000 house-and-land package in Byford, first home owners), c081 (a $1,300,000
-- townhouse at the general rate), c094 (a strata apartment, general rate); Jake k074 (a $390,000 apartment off the plan, single
-- first home buyer); Daniel d037 (a $1,600,000 apartment bought by a citizen and a permanent resident as joint tenants: any
-- foreign duty?), d055 (a $4,200,000 house, both citizens), d065 and d071 (share acquisitions of unlisted companies: duty only
-- if land-rich). c074 (vehicle licence duty) is in da-vehicles.l4. SCOPED to those questions and the definitions and
-- conditions needed to answer them.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: every other dutiable transaction and the dutiable value rules (ss 27-44A; the value is an input); exemptions,
-- nominal duty and other concessions (Part 6 Divisions 1, 2, 4); the off-the-plan concession (Chapter 6A), which may bear on
-- k074; the FHOG Act eligibility test itself (whether a transferee is a "concessional first home owner" is an INPUT, s 142A
-- borrows it from the First Home Owner Grant Act 2000) and the FHOG Act meaning of "home" (an input flag); the
-- metropolitan and Peel region boundaries (an input); further concessional transactions (s 142(2), 143(2)-(4)); the
-- reduction for excluded interests (s 189), linked entities (s 156-157), relevant arrangements (s 155(3)-(4)) and exemptions
-- for landholder duty; foreign landholder duty (Chapter 3A Part 3) and the foreign corporation and foreign trust tests.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Duties Act 2008 -- transfer duty and landholder duty`

§§ `s 26 and Schedule 2 Division 1 -- the general rate`

-- s 26(1): "Unless otherwise provided in this Chapter, duty is chargeable -- (a) by reference to the dutiable value of a
-- dutiable transaction; and (b) at the general rate of duty." (2): the rates "are set out in Schedule 2".
-- Schedule 2 Division 1, "Dutiable value (rounded down to nearest whole dollar)":
--   $0 - $120 000            $1.90 per $100 or part of $100
--   $120 001 - $150 000      $2 280 + $2.85 per $100 or part of $100 above $120 000
--   $150 001 - $360 000      $3 135 + $3.80 per $100 or part of $100 above $150 000
--   $360 001 - $725 000      $11 115 + $4.75 per $100 or part of $100 above $360 000
--   $725 001 and upwards     $28 453 + $5.15 per $100 or part of $100 above $725 000
-- (At $725 000 the fourth band gives $28 452.50; the fifth band starts from $28 453.)

GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of 100-dollar parts in` MEANS
    IF FLOOR (`amount` DIVIDED BY 100) TIMES 100 EQUALS `amount`
    THEN `amount` DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE FLOOR (`amount` DIVIDED BY 100) PLUS 1

GIVEN `whole dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the general rate on whole dollars` MEANS
    IF `whole dollars` AT MOST 120000
    THEN 1.90 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` `whole dollars`
    ELSE IF `whole dollars` AT MOST 150000
         THEN 2280 PLUS 2.85 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`whole dollars` MINUS 120000)
         ELSE IF `whole dollars` AT MOST 360000
              THEN 3135 PLUS 3.80 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`whole dollars` MINUS 150000)
              ELSE IF `whole dollars` AT MOST 725000
                   THEN 11115 PLUS 4.75 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`whole dollars` MINUS 360000)
                   ELSE 28453 PLUS 5.15 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`whole dollars` MINUS 725000)

GIVEN `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the duty at the general rate` MEANS
    `the general rate on whole dollars` (FLOOR (`the dutiable value`))

§§ `Chapter 2 Part 6 Division 3 -- first home owner concessional rate`

-- s 142A(1): a "concessional first home owner" is "(a) a transferee who is paid a first home owner grant in relation to the
-- property or to whom a first home owner grant is or will be payable in relation to the property; or (b) a transferee to whom a
-- first home owner grant would be, or would have been, payable" had consideration been given, or, for "an established home",
-- but for the FHOG Act s 14(5A). That test lives in the FHOG Act and is an INPUT here.
-- s 142(1): a first home owner concessional transaction is a transfer or agreement for transfer where "(a) ... each transferee
-- is a concessional first home owner" and "(b) the unencumbered value of the dutiable property ... does not exceed -- (i) if the
-- property is land that does not include a home -- $450 000; or (ii) if the property is land in the metropolitan region or
-- the Peel region that includes a home -- $700 000; or (iii) if the property is land outside the metropolitan region and the
-- Peel region that includes a home -- $750 000."
-- s 143(1): "Duty is chargeable on a first home owner concessional transaction at the applicable concessional rate of duty."
-- Schedule 2 Division 2, s 143 First home owners:
--   does not include a home:                 $0 - $350 000 Nil;  $350 001 - $450 000 $15.39 per $100 or part above $350 000
--   metropolitan or Peel, includes a home:   $0 - $500 000 Nil;  $500 001 - $700 000 $13.63 per $100 or part above $500 000
--   outside both, includes a home:           $0 - $500 000 Nil;  $500 001 - $750 000 $11.89 per $100 or part above $500 000
-- s 141(2): "If a term is given a meaning in the FHOG Act, it has the same meaning in this Division" -- so "home" is the FHOG
-- Act's word; whether the property "includes a home" is an INPUT.
-- Naive simplification: the test in s 142(1)(b) is on unencumbered value and the rate on dutiable value; one figure is used
-- for both.

DECLARE Location IS ONE OF
    `in the metropolitan or Peel region`
    `outside the metropolitan and Peel regions`

DECLARE `Home purchase` HAS
    `price` IS A NUMBER
    `includes a home` IS A BOOLEAN
    `where` IS A Location
    `each transferee is a concessional first home owner` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the purchase` IS A `Home purchase`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first home owner value cap` MEANS
    IF NOT `the purchase`'s `includes a home`
    THEN 450000
    ELSE CONSIDER `the purchase`'s `where`
         WHEN `in the metropolitan or Peel region` THEN 700000
         OTHERWISE 750000

GIVEN `the purchase` IS A `Home purchase`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a first home owner concessional transaction` IF
        `the purchase`'s `each transferee is a concessional first home owner`
    AND `the purchase`'s `price` AT MOST `the first home owner value cap` `the purchase`

GIVEN `the purchase` IS A `Home purchase`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first home owner concessional duty` MEANS
    IF NOT `the purchase`'s `includes a home`
    THEN (IF `whole` AT MOST 350000 THEN 0 ELSE 15.39 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`whole` MINUS 350000))
    ELSE CONSIDER `the purchase`'s `where`
         WHEN `in the metropolitan or Peel region`
             THEN (IF `whole` AT MOST 500000 THEN 0 ELSE 13.63 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`whole` MINUS 500000))
         OTHERWISE (IF `whole` AT MOST 500000 THEN 0 ELSE 11.89 TIMES `the number of 100-dollar parts in` (`whole` MINUS 500000))
    WHERE
        `whole` MEANS FLOOR (`the purchase`'s `price`)

GIVEN `the purchase` IS A `Home purchase`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the transfer duty on the purchase` MEANS
    IF `it is a first home owner concessional transaction` `the purchase`
    THEN `the first home owner concessional duty` `the purchase`
    ELSE `the duty at the general rate` (`the purchase`'s `price`)

§§ `Chapter 3A Part 2 -- foreign transfer duty`

-- s 205A(1): "foreign individual means an individual who is not -- (a) an Australian citizen as defined in the Australian
-- Citizenship Act 2007 (Commonwealth) section 3; or (b) the holder of a permanent visa as defined in the Migration Act 1958
-- (Commonwealth) section 5(1); or (c) the holder of a special category visa as defined in the Migration Act 1958
-- (Commonwealth) section 5(1)". A "foreign person" is a foreign corporation, a foreign individual or a foreign trustee.
-- s 205H(1)(b): a foreign dutiable transaction includes "an agreement ... for the transfer of residential property to a
-- foreign person". s 205G: foreign transfer duty "is imposed on foreign dutiable transactions".
-- s 205L: "joint tenants of residential property are taken to hold the property as tenants in common in equal shares."
-- s 205O: "Foreign transfer duty is chargeable at the rate of 7% of the dutiable value of the foreign dutiable transaction."
-- s 205K(1): liable if "(a) liable to pay transfer duty on the transaction; and (b) a foreign person."
-- INFERENCE (not stated in these words): for two joint tenants, each is taken to acquire half, and the 7% falls on the half
-- acquired by each foreign individual.

DECLARE Individual HAS
    `is an Australian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a permanent visa` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a special category visa` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a foreign individual` IF
        (NOT `the person`'s `is an Australian citizen`)
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `holds a permanent visa`)
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `holds a special category visa`)

GIVEN `the person` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A NUMBER
`one if foreign` MEANS
    IF `the person is a foreign individual` `the person` THEN 1 ELSE 0

GIVEN `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER, `residential` IS A BOOLEAN, `first joint tenant` IS AN Individual, `second joint tenant` IS AN Individual
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the foreign transfer duty on a joint purchase` MEANS
    IF NOT `residential`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the dutiable value` DIVIDED BY 2 TIMES 7 DIVIDED BY 100
         TIMES (`one if foreign` `first joint tenant` PLUS `one if foreign` `second joint tenant`)

§§ `s 15 -- dutiable property`

-- s 15: "Any of the following is dutiable property -- (a) land in Western Australia; (b) a right; (c) a chattel in Western
-- Australia; (d) a Western Australian business asset." Shares are not in the list; s 79's "business asset" lists goodwill,
-- restraints of trade, business identities, business licences, uncompleted supply rights and intellectual property, not
-- shares. (That a share is not a "chattel" is an INFERENCE from the ordinary meaning; s 3 says only what a chattel does not
-- include.)

DECLARE `Kind of property` IS ONE OF
    `land in Western Australia`
    `land outside Western Australia`
    `a right`
    `a chattel in Western Australia`
    `a Western Australian business asset`
    `shares in a company`

GIVEN `the property` IS A `Kind of property`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the property is dutiable property` IF
    CONSIDER `the property`
    WHEN `land outside Western Australia` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `shares in a company` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Chapter 3 -- landholder duty`

-- s 151: "Duty is imposed in respect of any relevant acquisition under Part 5 of an interest in an entity that under Part 4
-- is a landholder". s 152: an entity is a corporation or a unit trust scheme.
-- s 155(2): "An entity is a landholder if immediately before the acquisition -- (a) it is entitled to land assets in Western
-- Australia or an entity linked to the entity is so entitled; and (b) the total value of all such entitlements is
-- $2 000 000 or more." (s 155(3)-(4), relevant arrangements below the threshold, are not encoded.)
-- s 161: "significant interest ... (a) if the landholder is a listed landholder -- an interest of at least 90%; or
-- (b) otherwise -- an interest of at least 50%."
-- s 163(1)(a)/(b): crossing into a significant interest (the acquirer's own, or the aggregated group interest);
-- (c)/(d): already holding one and increasing it. Here the interest is the aggregated group interest, as a percentage.
-- s 184(1): duty "at the general rate of duty set out in Schedule 2". s 188(1), (3): the rate is applied "to the value of
-- the interest of the acquirer in the landholder immediately after the relevant acquisition", which is "the same percentage
-- of the value of the landholder as the percentage of the interest". s 186(1): the value of the landholder is the
-- unencumbered value of its WA land assets and chattels (plus linked entities' share -- an input here).
-- The s 189 reduction for excluded interests is NOT encoded.

DECLARE `Entity` HAS
    `is listed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `value of land assets in Western Australia` IS A NUMBER
    `value of land assets and chattels in Western Australia` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the entity` IS AN `Entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entity is a landholder` IF
    `the entity`'s `value of land assets in Western Australia` AT LEAST 2000000

GIVEN `the entity` IS AN `Entity`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the significant interest` MEANS
    IF `the entity`'s `is listed` THEN 90 ELSE 50

GIVEN `the entity` IS AN `Entity`, `interest before` IS A NUMBER, `interest after` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a relevant acquisition` IF
        `the entity is a landholder` `the entity`
    AND (    (`interest before` LESS THAN `the significant interest` `the entity`
              AND `interest after` AT LEAST `the significant interest` `the entity`)
         OR  (`interest before` AT LEAST `the significant interest` `the entity`
              AND `interest after` GREATER THAN `interest before`))

GIVEN `the entity` IS AN `Entity`, `interest before` IS A NUMBER, `interest after` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the landholder duty` MEANS
    IF `it is a relevant acquisition` `the entity` `interest before` `interest after`
    THEN `the duty at the general rate`
             (`the entity`'s `value of land assets and chattels in Western Australia` TIMES `interest after` DIVIDED BY 100)
    ELSE 0
